INFO:     127.0.0.1:64160 - "GET /api/feedback?node_id=&msg_id=%5B%22assistant%22%2C%22In%20the%20jagged%20crags%20of%20the%20Ironspire%20Mountains%2C%20Ignis%20was%20a%20dragon%20of%20legendary%20ferocity.%20For%20three%20centuries%2C%20his%20days%20were%20measured%20in%20scorched%20earth%20and%20looted%20gold.%20However%2C%20his%20life%20changed%20on%20a%20Tuesday%20in%202024%20(as%20recorded%20in%20*The%20Chronicles%20of%20the%20Ironspire*%2C%20published%202025)%20when%20he%20accidentally%20incinerated%20a%20wandering%20merchant%E2%80%99s%20wagon.%20Expecting%20gold%2C%20he%20found%20only%20a%20crate%20of%20rare%20spices%20and%20a%20cast-iron%20skillet%20that%20had%20miraculously%20survived%20the%20blaze.%20Intrigued%20by%20the%20scent%20of%20saffron%20and%20cumin%2C%20Ignis%20tasted%20a%20singed%20remnant%20of%20the%20merchant%27s%20inventory.%20The%20complexity%20of%20the%20flavor%E2%80%94a%20stark%20contrast%20to%20the%20monotonous%20char%20of%20scorched%20livestock%E2%80%94ignited%20a%20new%20obsession.%5Cn%5CnIgnis%20began%20his%20culinary%20journey%20by%20experimenting%20with%20thermal%20control.%20Dragons%20are%20accustomed%20to%20%5C%22all%20or%20nothing%5C%22%20fire%2C%20but%20cooking%20required%20precision.%20In%20a%20study%20titled%20%5C%22Dragon-Scale%20Thermodynamics%20and%20Culinary%20Applications%5C%22%20(published%202026)%2C%20researchers%20noted%20that%20Ignis%20spent%20months%20learning%20to%20regulate%20his%20internal%20furnace%2C%20mastering%20a%20gentle%2C%20lingering%20warmth%20that%20could%20caramelize%20onions%20without%20turning%20them%20to%20ash.%20He%20spent%20his%20nights%20in%20the%20valleys%2C%20stealthily%20observing%20village%20kitchens%20from%20the%20shadows%2C%20learning%20the%20intricate%20dance%20of%20chopping%2C%20seasoning%2C%20and%20simmering.%5Cn%5CnThe%20turning%20point%20came%20when%20he%20decided%20to%20recreate%20a%20complex%20bouillabaisse%20he%20had%20observed%20a%20tavern%20chef%20preparing%20in%20the%20summer%20of%202025%20(*Culinary%20Arts%20of%20the%20Northern%20Coast*%2C%20published%202026).%20He%20spent%20weeks%20perfecting%20his%20technique%2C%20using%20his%20immense%20claws%20as%20delicate%20whisks%20and%20his%20breath%20as%20a%20convection%20oven.%20When%20he%20finally%20served%20the%20dish%20to%20a%20group%20of%20terrified%20but%20hungry%20travelers%20he%20had%20%5C%22invited%5C%22%20to%20his%20lair%2C%20the%20feedback%20was%20transformative.%20The%20travelers%2C%20initially%20fearing%20for%20their%20lives%2C%20found%20the%20flavor%20profile%20to%20be%20of%20Michelin-star%20quality.%5Cn%5CnWord%20of%20the%20%5C%22Gourmet%20Dragon%5C%22%20spread%20quickly.%20By%20early%202026%2C%20Ignis%20had%20transitioned%20from%20a%20terror%20of%20the%20skies%20to%20the%20most%20exclusive%20chef%20in%20the%20realm.%20According%20to%20a%20feature%20in%20the%20*Gastronomic%20Gazette*%20(published%20March%202026)%2C%20his%20lair%20became%20a%20pilgrimage%20site%20for%20food%20critics.%20Ignis%20eventually%20traded%20his%20hoard%20of%20gold%20for%20a%20massive%2C%20custom-built%20kitchen%20forged%20from%20volcanic%20rock%2C%20proving%20that%20even%20the%20most%20destructive%20force%20can%20find%20purpose%20in%20the%20delicate%20art%20of%20seasoning.%20He%20remains%20active%20today%2C%20with%20his%20signature%20%5C%22Dragon-Fire%20Roasted%20Vegetables%5C%22%20cited%20as%20the%20most%20sought-after%20dish%20of%20the%20year%20in%20the%20*International%20Food%20Review*%20(published%20September%202026).%22%2Cnull%2Cnull%2Cfalse%2Cnull%5D&session_id=ct-62835637 HTTP/1.1" 200 OK
