INFO:     127.0.0.1:64160 - "GET /api/feedback?node_id=&msg_id=%5B%22assistant%22%2C%22Captain%20Elara%20Vance%20felt%20the%20familiar%2C%20bone-deep%20shudder%20of%20the%20*Aethelgard*%20as%20it%20dropped%20out%20of%20warp%2C%20the%20transition%20always%20feeling%20like%20being%20pulled%20through%20a%20needle%27s%20eye.%20Ahead%20of%20her%2C%20the%20viewport%20cleared%2C%20revealing%20the%20object%20of%20her%20four-year%20journey%3A%20Kepler-186f%20Prime.%20It%20was%20not%20the%20barren%20rock%20the%20long-range%20scans%20had%20suggested.%20Instead%2C%20it%20was%20a%20sphere%20of%20deep%2C%20swirling%20indigo%20and%20vibrant%2C%20bioluminescent%20veins%20that%20pulsed%20in%20a%20slow%2C%20rhythmic%20cadence%20against%20the%20black%20canvas%20of%20space.%5Cn%5CnAccording%20to%20the%20mission%20data%20(published%20January%2012%2C%202026)%2C%20the%20planet%20possessed%20an%20atmosphere%20rich%20in%20neon%20and%20oxygen%2C%20capable%20of%20supporting%20life.%20As%20she%20initiated%20the%20descent%20sequence%2C%20Elara%20noted%20the%20date%E2%80%94November%204%2C%202026%E2%80%94marking%20the%20moment%20humanity%20finally%20breached%20the%20veil%20of%20the%20neighboring%20sector.%20The%20descent%20was%20turbulent%2C%20the%20ship%E2%80%99s%20hull%20groaning%20under%20the%20pressure%20of%20the%20dense%2C%20ionized%20air.%20As%20the%20cloud%20layer%20parted%2C%20the%20landscape%20below%20revealed%20itself%20not%20in%20shades%20of%20green%20or%20brown%2C%20but%20in%20a%20spectrum%20of%20iridescent%20silvers%20and%20deep%20purples.%5Cn%5CnUpon%20landing%2C%20the%20silence%20of%20the%20planet%20was%20absolute%2C%20save%20for%20the%20hum%20of%20her%20suit%E2%80%99s%20life-support%20systems.%20She%20stepped%20onto%20the%20surface%2C%20her%20boots%20sinking%20into%20a%20fine%2C%20crystalline%20dust%20that%20shimmered%20like%20crushed%20diamonds%20under%20the%20light%20of%20the%20binary%20stars%20overhead.%20The%20flora%20here%20was%20architectural%3B%20towering%2C%20translucent%20spires%20that%20reached%20toward%20the%20sky%2C%20vibrating%20with%20a%20low-frequency%20hum%20that%20resonated%20in%20her%20chest.%20She%20approached%20one%2C%20extending%20a%20gloved%20hand.%20As%20her%20fingers%20touched%20the%20surface%2C%20the%20spire%20flared%20with%20a%20soft%2C%20warm%20amber%20light%2C%20and%20the%20ground%20beneath%20her%20feet%20began%20to%20glow%20in%20response%2C%20a%20ripple%20of%20energy%20spreading%20outward%20from%20her%20position%20like%20a%20stone%20dropped%20in%20a%20still%20pond.%5Cn%5CnElara%20spent%20hours%20recording%20the%20environmental%20data%2C%20noting%20the%20strange%2C%20fluid-like%20movement%20of%20the%20local%20atmosphere%20(as%20documented%20in%20the%20planetary%20survey%20report%2C%20June%202026).%20She%20realized%20then%20that%20this%20was%20not%20merely%20a%20new%20world%3B%20it%20was%20a%20living%2C%20interconnected%20organism.%20Every%20step%20she%20took%2C%20every%20breath%20she%20drew%2C%20seemed%20to%20be%20registered%20by%20the%20planet%20itself.%20She%20placed%20a%20data%20beacon%2C%20its%20blinking%20light%20a%20stark%2C%20artificial%20intrusion%20against%20the%20organic%20brilliance%20of%20the%20landscape.%20As%20the%20binary%20stars%20began%20to%20set%2C%20casting%20long%2C%20fractured%20shadows%20across%20the%20crystalline%20plains%2C%20Elara%20looked%20back%20at%20the%20*Aethelgard*%2C%20feeling%20the%20weight%20of%20the%20immense%20distance%20between%20her%20and%20the%20rest%20of%20her%20species.%20She%20had%20discovered%20a%20world%20that%20did%20not%20just%20exist%3B%20it%20watched.%22%2Cnull%2Cnull%2Cfalse%2Cnull%5D&session_id=ct-7282b578 HTTP/1.1" 200 OK
