INFO:     127.0.0.1:53663 - "GET /api/feedback?node_id=&msg_id=%5B%22assistant%22%2C%22As%20an%20AI%20assistant%2C%20I%20do%20not%20have%20a%20persistent%20background%20daemon%2C%20a%20cron%20scheduler%2C%20or%20hardware-level%20self-wake%20capabilities.%20Any%20prior%20mention%20of%20a%20%5C%22self-wake%20capability%5C%22%20refers%20to%20the%20architectural%20design%20of%20the%20underlying%20platform%20rather%20than%20an%20active%20background%20process%20running%20on%20your%20local%20machine.%5Cn%5Cn%23%23%23%20Platform%20Architecture%20and%20Self-Wake%20Concepts%5Cn%5Cn-%20**Background%20Scheduler%3A**%20In%20certain%20enterprise%20deployment%20models%2C%20platforms%20utilize%20external%20orchestration%20layers%20(such%20as%20Kubernetes%20CronJobs%20or%20cloud-native%20event%20triggers)%20to%20wake%20sleeping%20instances%20when%20specific%20webhook%20events%20or%20time-based%20triggers%20occur.%20However%2C%20within%20the%20direct%20scope%20of%20local%20script%20execution%20and%20interactive%20sessions%2C%20this%20layer%20is%20managed%20by%20the%20host%20environment.%5Cn-%20**The%20Operator%20Flag%3A**%20When%20configuring%20automated%20agents%2C%20an%20operator%20flag%20(such%20as%20%60--allow-background%60%20or%20explicit%20execution%20permissions)%20dictates%20whether%20a%20process%20is%20permitted%20to%20re-initialize%20autonomously%20upon%20receiving%20a%20scheduled%20payload.%20Without%20this%20flag%20explicitly%20enabled%20in%20the%20runtime%20environment%2C%20the%20system%20remains%20entirely%20reactive%20to%20direct%20user%20prompts.%5Cn-%20**%60schedule_task%60%20as%20the%20Active%20Alternative%3A**%20Because%20autonomous%20self-waking%20is%20restricted%20or%20absent%20in%20standard%20interactive%20contexts%2C%20**%60schedule_task%60**%20serves%20as%20the%20active%2C%20programmatic%20alternative.%20Instead%20of%20the%20system%20waking%20itself%20up%20independently%2C%20%60schedule_task%60%20explicitly%20registers%20a%20future%20execution%20event%20within%20the%20system%27s%20task%20queue%20or%20scheduler%20service%2C%20ensuring%20that%20a%20designated%20script%20or%20function%20runs%20at%20a%20specified%20future%20timestamp%20or%20interval.%22%2Cnull%2Cnull%2Cfalse%2Cnull%5D&session_id=c-c82e3517 HTTP/1.1" 200 OK
